      "text": "**The air doesn’t look too bad for most people, but I’d wait to jog right now because George Town is currently under a thundershower.** The latest nearby Malaysian DOE reading I found was **API 67 (moderate) at 3 p.m.**; a live George Town monitor showed **US AQI 93**, also moderate but near the upper end. Readings can vary by area. ([jerebumalaysia.com](https://jerebumalaysia.com/en/stations/minden-pulau-pinang/))\n\nOnce the storm has passed, an easy jog should be reasonable if you’re generally healthy. If you have asthma or heart/lung disease, or you notice haze or breathing irritation, take it indoors; check your local reading again before heading out. ([iqair.com](https://www.iqair.com/as/air-quality/malaysia/penang))",
